# .gitleaksignore
# Allowlist for gitleaks false-positives.
# Each line is a SHA256 fingerprint of a specific finding to suppress.
#
# Intentional documentation suppressions:
# - security/secret-scan-report.md:  documents previously found secrets for audit purposes
# - security/git-history-cleanup.md: lists historic leaked values for cleanup tracking
# - TEST_CREDENTIALS.md:             local-dev test credentials document (not for prod)
#
# To add a new fingerprint, run:
#   gitleaks detect --report-format json --report-path report.json
# then copy the "Fingerprint" field from the relevant finding.
#
# Suppressions for legacy doc references (security audit report + history cleanup guide)
# These files exist solely to document what was found and remediated.
# Format: <fingerprint>
